// 소스를 연 채로 인용을 적는다. 요약이 아니라 원문과 그 위치다.
{"id":"e1","source":"w1","locator":"§intro","quote":"At a high level, I found that effort was a great way of modulating how much verification and edgecase testing Claude did and how much of its own judgement it used.","why":"w1 의 결론 한 줄: effort 가 바꾸는 것은 검증과 판단의 양"}
{"id":"e2","source":"w1","locator":"§What is effort?","quote":"At a high level, effort gives the model an approximation of how much compute you want it to spend on the task.","why":"effort 의 정의"}
{"id":"e3","source":"w1","locator":"§What is effort?","quote":"Claude will always try and do your task reasonably, but higher effort will involve Claude taking more independent action for judgement and verification.","why":"높은 effort 가 더하는 것: 독립 판단과 검증"}
{"id":"e4","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort curves, FIG A aria-label","quote":"Opus 5.5 scores highest at every setting, from 36.6% at low to 65.7% at max","why":"Terminal-Bench 3.0 에서 Opus 5.5 의 low→max 통과율"}
{"id":"e5","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort curves, FIG A aria-label","quote":"Opus 5.5 at high matches Fable 5.1 at max (58.9% against 58.0%) on half the tokens.","why":"모델과 effort 의 교환: 큰 단계보다 다른 모델이 싸게 같은 점수"}
{"id":"e6","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort curves, FIG A aria-label","quote":"Fable 5 levels off at 43.4% from xhigh to max.","why":"단계를 올려도 평평해지는 곡선의 예"}
{"id":"e7","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort curves, FIG A caption","quote":"Terminal-Bench 3.0, the same 70 tasks for every model (the 4 GPU tasks are left out). Opus 5.5 ran about three weeks later, with responses capped at 128k tokens and no GitHub or PyPI access; Opus 5’s max is its effort-120 run.","why":"그림 A 의 조건"}
{"id":"e8","source":"w1","locator":"§Building with effort / Underspecified build task","quote":"At low effort, the fitness app is just a log and a simple graph. At higher effort levels the app is more complex with additional detail. At max effort there’s a heat chart.","why":"덜 정해진 과제에서 단계가 결과물의 범위를 바꾼다"}
{"id":"e9","source":"w1","locator":"§Underspecified build task, figure tabs","quote":"low(1.5 min)medium(4 min)high(11 min)max(67 min)","why":"단계별 소요 시간, 한 줄 프롬프트 빌드"}
{"id":"e10","source":"w1","locator":"§Lightly specified design task","quote":"At low effort (which took 1 minute), I got an interactive sketch that conveyed the idea but didn’t look very much like Claude Code.","why":"/config 재설계 low"}
{"id":"e11","source":"w1","locator":"§Lightly specified design task","quote":"At max effort (which took 28 minutes), I got a mockup that looked very much like Claude Code, along with a bunch of walkthroughs for different flows.","why":"/config 재설계 max"}
{"id":"e12","source":"w1","locator":"§Highly specified build task","quote":"I found that given this spec, the models behaved much more similarly.","why":"명세가 자세하면 단계 차이가 줄어든다"}
{"id":"e13","source":"w1","locator":"§Highly specified build task, figure tabs","quote":"low(16 min)medium(22 min)high(33 min)max(79 min)","why":"명세 빌드의 단계별 시간"}
{"id":"e14","source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"Low effort allows Claude to respond quickly with a starting point, higher effort levels will get more work done but Claude will also make more assumptions on my behalf.","why":"높은 단계의 대가: 사용자 대신 가정을 더 한다"}
{"id":"e15","source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"Give Claude a spec and ask it to interview me about any details I’m missing","why":"w1 의 기능 개발 루프 1단계"}
{"id":"e16","source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"Review to make sure it got the gist of it correct, iterate on low effort as needed","why":"루프 3단계"}
{"id":"e17","source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"Verify and test on high effort","why":"루프 4단계"}
{"id":"e18","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"My main takeaway from reading the Terminal-Bench 3.0 results was that higher effort is best for tasks with lots of hidden edge cases.","why":"높은 단계가 맞는 과제의 조건"}
{"id":"e19","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"Fable 5.1 went from 1/5 at low to 5/5 at xhigh.","why":"html-js-filter 결과"}
{"id":"e20","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"A typical attempt at low effort takes about 2 minutes. Each of these attempts wrote a filter in roughly one pass, then tested it against a single hand-written page.","why":"low 에서 실제로 한 일"}
{"id":"e21","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"A high-effort run finishes in about 33 minutes. In the run I traced, it adversarially reviewed its first draft, then read the installed parser’s source to check for bugs","why":"high 에서 실제로 더 한 일"}
{"id":"e22","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"Overall, increasing effort tends to reduce failures due to missing edgecases (purple blocks), but does not fix when the model has the wrong approach (blue blocks).","why":"effort 가 고치는 실패와 못 고치는 실패"}
{"id":"e23","source":"w1","locator":"FIG B svg text","quote":"Fable 5.1 at low 370 attempts, median 73k tokens each Fable 5.1 at max 370 attempts, median 222k tokens each passed 140 → 214 missed a case 59 → 24","why":"Fable 5.1 low→max 의 통과·토큰·놓친 경우"}
{"id":"e24","source":"w1","locator":"FIG B svg text","quote":"made the wrong call 133 → 107","why":"잘못된 판단 계열은 적게 준다"}
{"id":"e25","source":"w1","locator":"FIG B svg text","quote":"picked the wrong reading 25 → 47","why":"max 에서 오히려 늘어난 실패 종류"}
{"id":"e26","source":"w1","locator":"FIG B svg text","quote":"a bug its tests missed 40 → 14","why":"테스트가 놓친 버그는 크게 준다"}
{"id":"e27","source":"w1","locator":"FIG B caption","quote":"Each square is one attempt. Failure kinds come from a model judge and are approximate.","why":"실패 분류의 한계"}
{"id":"e28","source":"w1","locator":"FIG C svg text","quote":"Security 64% → 87%, Hardware 34% → 75%, ML 54% → 73%, Science 41% → 61%, Software 43% → 56%, Media 18% → 30%, Operations 12% → 22%","why":"분야별 low→top 통과율, Fable 5.1"}
{"id":"e29","source":"w1","locator":"FIG C caption","quote":"Pass rate. Low effort pools each model's two lowest settings, top effort its three highest, since categories are small.","why":"그림 C 의 low/top 정의"}
{"id":"e30","source":"w1","locator":"FIG C aria-label","quote":"Hardware, 5 tasks. Fable 5.1 passes 34 percent at low effort and 75 percent at top effort.","why":"분야마다 과제 수가 작다"}
{"id":"e31","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"At low (about a minute per attempt), Claude would edit the code before building it or running the reproducer, and did not check that its new test would have caught the original bug.","why":"mvcc-lsm-compaction low 의 행동"}
{"id":"e32","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"At xhigh (about 11 minutes), Claude reproduced the crash first, wrote a randomized test against a reference that never compacts, and checked that its tests failed on half-finished fixes.","why":"xhigh 의 행동"}
{"id":"e33","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"Opus 5.5 went from 0/5 at low to 4/5 at xhigh.","why":"mvcc-lsm-compaction 결과"}
{"id":"e34","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"The low attempts wrote a solver in one pass, checked it with a few small problems and stopped around 10k tokens. In the final message, Claude warned it might be slow on big problems, but did not check.","why":"cli-2ph-simplex low: 경고만 하고 확인 안 함"}
{"id":"e35","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"Opus 5.5 went from 0/5 at low to 5/5 at high.","why":"cli-2ph-simplex 결과"}
{"id":"e36","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"At high, Claude tried two ways of prepping the data, noticed that the list of significant treatments changed, and dug into why before choosing the correct one.","why":"gsea-proteomics high 의 행동"}
{"id":"e37","source":"w1","locator":"§Problem areas where effort helps","quote":"If a user were in the loop, Claude may have asked the user about the way to set up the problem, but without a user in the loop, high effort does better.","why":"사람이 루프에 있는지가 단계 선택을 바꾼다"}
{"id":"e38","source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels in Claude Code","quote":"Low: for when I want quick responses that are in the loop, e.g. brainstorming, sketching, easy changes","why":"규칙 low"}
{"id":"e39","source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels in Claude Code","quote":"Medium: for most of my regular software engineering work, e.g. new feature implementation.","why":"규칙 medium"}
{"id":"e40","source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels in Claude Code","quote":"High: for work where verification is important or there are edge cases, e.g. fixing a bug in a brownfield codebase.","why":"규칙 high"}
{"id":"e41","source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels in Claude Code","quote":"Max: When I want Claude to operate fully autonomously to solve difficult problems, e.g. end to end building and verification of an app, finding security vulnerabilities in critical software.","why":"규칙 max"}
{"id":"e42","source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels in Claude Code","quote":"Try varying effort for Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 based on your task or even mid-conversation by using /effort in Claude Code","why":"Claude Code 의 /effort 명령"}
{"id":"e43","source":"w1","locator":"footnote ¹","quote":"these come from our own internal runs, 5 attempts per task, with our production safety interventions off for Fable 5.1","why":"숫자의 출처와 조건"}
{"id":"e44","source":"w1","locator":"footnote ¹","quote":"The worked examples come from individual runs, some at intermediate effort settings.","why":"예시는 개별 실행"}
{"id":"e45","source":"w1","locator":"§intro","quote":"One of the best parts of our newest Claude models is how they respond to effort without breaking the prompt cache in Claude Code","why":"Claude Code 에서 단계를 바꿔도 캐시가 유지된다는 주장"}
{"id":"e46","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"is the main control for how much Claude Opus 5.5 thinks, and because thinking is always on, it's the first setting to adjust when trading off intelligence, latency, and cost.","why":"w2 의 effort 정의 (문장 머리의 Effort 는 markdown 링크라 뺐다)"}
{"id":"e47","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"Start at `medium`, the default on Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Opus 5 defaults to `high`), set it explicitly, and test several levels against your own evals rather than carrying over the setting you used on Claude Opus 5.","why":"재는 법의 출발점"}
{"id":"e48","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"Effort level names don't correspond to the same amount of thinking across models","why":"모델이 바뀌면 같은 이름이 다른 양"}
{"id":"e49","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"in Anthropic's testing, Claude Opus 5.5 at `medium` matches or exceeds Claude Opus 5 at `high` on coding and knowledge-work evaluations, and on several coding evaluations `low` comes close to it at much lower cost.","why":"medium 기본값의 근거"}
{"id":"e50","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶2","quote":"At a given level, Claude Opus 5.5 tends to think more per turn than Claude Opus 5, especially at `xhigh` and `max`.","why":"같은 단계에서 더 생각한다"}
{"id":"e51","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort bullet 1","quote":"Thinking counts toward `max_tokens` even when thinking content isn't returned to you","why":"max_tokens 주의"}
{"id":"e52","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort bullet 1","quote":"For the long turns that agentic coding can produce, a `max_tokens` of 128,000, the model's maximum, has worked well in Anthropic's testing.","why":"max_tokens 권장"}
{"id":"e53","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort bullet 2","quote":"Reserve `xhigh` and `max` for work where you've measured a quality gain.","why":"상위 단계는 잰 뒤에"}
{"id":"e54","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort bullet 3","quote":"Lowering effort reduces thinking, and with it cost and latency, more reliably than prompt instructions do.","why":"생각을 줄이려면 프롬프트보다 단계"}
{"id":"e55","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶3","quote":"Changing the top-level `effort` value between requests invalidates the prompt cache.","why":"API 수준 캐시 규칙"}
{"id":"e56","source":"w2","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶3","quote":"A change holds for every later turn until another one replaces it.","why":"대화 중 변경은 이후 턴에 계속 적용"}
{"id":"e57","source":"w2","locator":"§Capabilities relevant to prompting","quote":"In Anthropic's testing, at its default `medium` effort the model matched or beat Claude Opus 5 at `high` effort on such tasks, in fewer steps and with fewer tokens.","why":"에이전트 코딩에서 medium 의 근거"}
{"id":"e58","source":"w3","locator":"Key takeaways","quote":"It controls how much work Claude does on your request overall including the number of files read, tools used, and how many steps it takes before it checks back in with you.","why":"w3 의 effort 정의: 생각 시간 이상"}
{"id":"e59","source":"w3","locator":"§Claude Code effort level and model selection","quote":"At lower effort, it would rather ask you for more context than spend tokens figuring something out on its own.","why":"낮은 단계는 되묻는다"}
{"id":"e60","source":"w3","locator":"§How Claude Code effort level works","quote":"These are all ordinary output tokens from the same loop, billed at the same rate.","why":"thinking 도 출력 토큰"}
{"id":"e61","source":"w3","locator":"§How Claude Code effort level works","quote":"The effort level is sent to the model as part of the request, right alongside your prompt.","why":"effort 의 전달 방식"}
{"id":"e62","source":"w3","locator":"§How Claude Code effort level works","quote":"Same prompt, two effort levels. The high effort path generates roughly 7x more tokens to reach a higher confidence answer.","why":"그림 캡션의 7배 (예시)"}
{"id":"e63","source":"w3","locator":"§How Claude Code effort level works","quote":"Claude will be more predisposed to double-checking additional hypotheses or verifying correctness at higher effort levels, but it generally won’t artificially inflate usage for simple tasks at higher effort levels.","why":"높은 단계가 단순 과제에서 부풀리지 않는다"}
{"id":"e64","source":"w3","locator":"§Picking an effort level","quote":"Our guidance is that for most tasks you should use the model’s default effort level.","why":"기본값 권장"}
{"id":"e65","source":"w3","locator":"§Picking an effort level","quote":"Consider this more as a general preference than a task-by-task decision.","why":"과제마다가 아니라 일의 종류마다"}
{"id":"e66","source":"w3","locator":"§What to change when Claude gets it wrong","quote":"If you're increasing effort on a task that shouldn't need it, the fix is often upstream, in your context, your CLAUDE.md, or how the task is scoped.","why":"단계 전에 맥락"}
{"id":"e67","source":"w3","locator":"§What to change when Claude gets it wrong","quote":"did it not try hard enough, or did it not know enough?","why":"진단 질문"}
{"id":"e68","source":"w3","locator":"§Effort: Claude didn’t try hard enough","quote":"Pick a higher effort level if Claude got it wrong by skipping a file, not running the tests, or not double-checking its work.","why":"effort 를 올릴 신호"}
{"id":"e69","source":"w3","locator":"Key takeaways","quote":"If Claude has all the pertinent context, clearly tried, and still got it wrong, that's a signal to pick a more capable model.","why":"모델을 바꿀 신호"}
{"id":"e70","source":"w3","locator":"§Effort, model, and token consumption","quote":"effort shapes token consumption but doesn't limit it. The only hard cap in the system is max_tokens","why":"effort 는 상한이 아니다"}
{"id":"e71","source":"w3","locator":"§Effort, model, and token consumption","quote":"The key point in the graphs above is that effort level picks how far Claude is willing to travel along the curve, but again, that doesn’t mean Claude will need to travel that far to complete the task.","why":"단계는 갈 수 있는 거리"}
{"id":"e72","source":"w3","locator":"§Picking an effort level","quote":"in our testing we found when you use the default effort setting for Opus 4.8, it will produce better results for about the same number of tokens when compared to using the default effort setting of Opus 4.7 for the same task.","why":"w3 가 다루는 모델 세대 (Opus 5.5 이전)"}
{"id":"e73","source":"w3","locator":"§Effort, model, and token consumption","quote":"Curves are for illustration purposes only, shown for a single task simple enough to be accomplished quickly by both models. They do not represent real benchmark data.","why":"w3 그림은 실측 아님"}
{"id":"e74","source":"w3","locator":"§Start with the defaults, then reach for the dials","quote":"Most of the time, you shouldn't be thinking about either setting.","why":"기본값 우선"}
{"id":"e75","source":"w1","locator":"§What is effort?","quote":"If someone asked you to do the same task in 1 hour, you’d try to get them the best version that meets their task and then expect to iterate from there.","why":"w1 의 시간 비유"}
{"id":"e76","source":"w1","locator":"§Lightly specified design task","quote":"For this particular task, I think I prefer using low effort to understand Claude’s vision.","why":"저자가 low 를 고른 이유"}
{"id":"e77","source":"w1","locator":"§Higher effort levels help when there are many edge cases","quote":"But you don’t need this level of effort for every task.","why":"높은 단계를 모든 과제에 쓰지 않는다"}
{"id":"e78","source":"w1","locator":"footnote ¹","quote":"The security tasks also ran without internet access, so the per-task counts here won’t line up with the public leaderboard or the launch post.","why":"공개 리더보드와 다름"}
